00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:18.360
So how is it we have a second brain?

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:24.600
Well the enteric nervous system is so complex
and contains so many nodes that it can act

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:30.370
as a neural network and process information
exactly like our brain does.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:36.110
So your gut isn't just reporting facts, it's
thinking them up too.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:41.630
Now, our second brain can't compose music
or help us out with our maths homework but

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:45.650
it can certainly think for itself.

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:50.020
One area it excels in is hormones and emotions.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:56.690
The gut contains 95% of the body's supply
of serotonin, a neurotransmitter that affects

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:02.290
our mood, it can make up happy, sad, anxious
and an array of other emotions.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:07.990
The gut is therefore hugely responsible for
controlling your mood.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:10.090
Happy gut, happy mind.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:17.310
So much so that there is even talk of medication
that directly targets your gut as a potential

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.110
cure for depression.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:26.880
But the key emotion here is anxiety and it's
how your gut can predict the future and often

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:32.190
make better decisions about a situation than
your actual brain.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:37.430
The enteric nervous system can make your brain
feel anxiety at the drop of a hat but it doesn't

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.210
just do it for fun.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:45.300
Our brain is constantly taking in massive
amounts of data and I mean MASSIVE.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:51.360
The brain processes 400 Billion bits of information
per second.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:57.060
The colours and shapes of every single object
in our surroundings, every sound we can hear,

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:00.640
the temperature, what we're going to say next.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:07.520
400 Billion bits of information at a time
sounds like superhuman levels of cognition

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.940
and it is.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:15.940
Because unfortunately, our conscious mind
is only aware of a measly 2,000 of these 400

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.910
billion bits of information.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:24.510
That means out of every 200 million bits of
information our brain takes in and processes,

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.150
we only pay attention to one of them.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:32.510
It's why experience tunnel vision or single-mindedness.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:37.350
Although our conscious mind doesn't make use
of those 400 billion bits of information,

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.230
our gut does.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:45.850
The enteric nervous system and the brain can
work together to deduce things from the constant

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:51.800
tidal-wave of ignored information and using
this collective information, the brain and

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:58.750
the gut, together can actually predict the
immediate future.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:03.950
And if the future looks somewhat uneasy our
gut immediately responds by making us feel

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:06.380
anxious.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:10.800
Researchers in Columbia carried out experiments
and stumbled upon something they called the

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.250
"emotional oracle effect".

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:18.390
Over eight separate studies test participants
were asked to make predictions on various

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:24.440
topics, such as who will be the next US president,
which movies will win awards, will the Dow

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:29.200
Jones index go up or down and even the weather.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:34.099
Some of the participants trusted their initial
gut feeling, whilst others made an educated

00:08:34.099 --> 00:08:38.169
and calculated guess based on their knowledge.

00:08:38.169 --> 00:08:44.480
72% of people who trusted their gut instinct
predicted that Barack Obama would beat Hilary

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:49.180
Clinton for the 2008 Democratic nomination.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:56.250
Whilst only 64% of people who actually put
thought into it made the same, correct prediction.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:01.899
At the time the two candidates were neck and
neck in the polls.

00:09:01.899 --> 00:09:08.920
In fact the gut instinct trusters were significantly
better at all the predictions than those who

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.740
thought about it logically.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:17.810
They were 25% better at predicting the Dow
Jones Index and they could even predict the

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:23.230
weather with some degree of accuracy, using
nothing more than what their enteric nervous

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.500
system was telling them.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:31.740
But the researchers found that this amazing
stomach-powered predictive talent only works

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:37.430
if the individual has at least some knowledge
of the situation, our gut feeling doesn't

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:41.020
work for things we know absolutely nothing
about.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:47.000
Suggesting that the test participants weren't
actually predicting the future in a supernatural

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:53.120
sense, but their enteric nervous system and
brain were collectively using their aggregated

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:58.250
knowledge to quickly form the most accurate
prediction possible.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:06.410
All those billions of bits of information
we take in each second are collectively summarised

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:12.160
and these summaries are sent to our enteric
nervous system, which uses it to determine

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:18.540
which emotion we should feel in our gut, anxiety,
fear, happiness?

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:23.410
Remember in school when the teacher left the
classroom for a few minutes and all hell broke

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:27.170
loose, you could guarantee that within five
seconds, someone would be stood on top of

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:30.980
a desk or drawing phallic images on the chalk
board.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:36.449
But then suddenly you got a gut feeling that
the teacher was returning, you couldn't hear

00:10:36.449 --> 00:10:42.540
them, but nevertheless, out of nowhere a wave
of silence and obedience would wash over the

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:45.610
classroom in an instant.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:49.689
Then the teacher would walk in, none-the-wiser.

00:10:49.689 --> 00:10:55.269
It's almost as if we predicted the future,
or our gut did anyway.

00:10:55.269 --> 00:11:00.579
You may have had the exact same experience
at work, when you're watching Thoughty2 on

00:11:00.579 --> 00:11:05.399
YouTube and suddenly, you sense that the boss
is walking down the hallway about to enter

00:11:05.399 --> 00:11:11.019
the room and rumble you, so you quickly hit
the like button and close your browser.

00:11:11.019 --> 00:11:16.740
Whilst this seems very mystical, it's not,
your brain and enteric nervous system are

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:22.790
actually using billions of bits of data and
past knowledge to make an educated guess at

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:28.040
the typical behavioural patterns of your teacher
or boss.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:32.300
Whilst your conscious mind is too distracted
with whatever is presently happening in front

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:33.300
of you.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:37.980
Perhaps your boss always comes and checks
on you around the same time each day, but

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:44.800
you've never realised, you don't look at the
clock, but your unconscious mind has, and

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:50.249
it has created a schedule of your boss's daily
actions and stored it at the back of your

00:11:50.249 --> 00:11:54.080
brain, without you even realising it.

00:11:54.080 --> 00:12:00.771
So it seems Petrov's lack of action on that
day he saved the world wasn't random, he may

00:12:00.771 --> 00:12:07.330
not have known why at the time, but there
will have been good reasons that his gut decided

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:13.430
to signal to him that something was amiss
with the alarm system, perhaps his unconscious

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:18.990
brain had picked up a few subtle signals from
his environment and past knowledge, that the

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:21.430
computers were malfunctioning.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:27.540
Petrov has later reflected back on the events
of that monumental day and he himself said

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:36.279
that, at the time, he had no idea why he didn't
report it to his superiors, he just felt it

00:12:36.279 --> 00:12:39.879
was wrong, but couldn't explain why.

00:12:39.879 --> 00:12:45.010
Looking back now he says there were definite
reasons why he should have suspected a false

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:52.420
alarm, such as, five or six missiles seemed
like an illogical first strike by the US,

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:58.110
compared to America's total arsenal that is
a tiny number of missiles and if you want

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:04.430
to suppress your opponent's chances of retaliation,
surely you would use your full nuclear force

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.139
against them upfront.

00:13:06.139 --> 00:13:12.810
It's little things like this that Petrov's
gut will have picked up on that day, but his

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:15.699
conscious mind wouldn't have.

00:13:15.699 --> 00:13:26.040
So yes, a man's stomach really did save the
world.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:40.920
Thanks for watching.

